*.tar
build_initrd/
.claude/
nyx_build_last.log
# Build.sh / Build-std.sh output when redirected here.
build_*.log

# A LITERAL `~` directory. A shell that does not expand `~` (PowerShell, cmd) turns
# `git clone … ~/foo` into a real folder named `~` inside the repo — and `git add -A` then stages it
# as an embedded git repository. This has now happened twice.
~/

# ★ Quantum provider credentials (IonQ / IBM API keys + the IBM instance CRN).
#
# Build.sh bakes this into the boot image so the keys reach the machine with nothing to type — Nyx
# has no clipboard and cannot express a paste chord, and an IBM CRN is ~120 characters.
#
# It must NEVER be committed: `git log -p` keeps a deleted line forever, and a leaked key on a
# metered quantum backend is someone else's bill. `quantum-credentials.example.txt` is the tracked
# template — copy it, do not rename it.
quantum-credentials.txt

# musl build outputs (reproducible via ./Build-musl.sh in ~90s)
vendor/musl/obj/
vendor/musl/lib/
vendor/musl/config.mak
vendor/musl/_install/

